  "content": {
    "id": "p27-q7-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "7",
    "prompt": "For each of the following functions, state the value(s) of $x$ for which $f(x)$ is stationary.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p27-q7-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$y=8x-x^2$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=4$",
          "worked": "$$y'=8-2x$$\n\nAt a stationary point, $y'=0$. $$\\begin{align*}8-2x&=0\\\\x&=4\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 13
      },
      {
        "id": "p27-q7-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$y=2x^3+3x^2-36x$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=-3$ or $x=2$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}y'&=6x^2+6x-36\\\\y'&=6(x+3)(x-2)\\end{align*}$$ At a stationary point, $y'=0$. $$\\begin{align*}6(x+3)(x-2)&=0\\\\x&=-3\\quad\\text{or}\\quad x=2\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 16
      },
      {
        "id": "p27-q7-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$y=x-\\sqrt{x}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=\\frac{1}{4}$",
          "worked": "For $x>0$, $$y'=1-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}}.$$ Set $y'=0$. $$\\begin{align*}1-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}}&=0\\\\2\\sqrt{x}&=1\\\\\\sqrt{x}&=\\frac12\\\\x&=\\frac14\\end{align*}$$ The derivative is undefined at $x=0$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 23
      },
      {
        "id": "p27-q7-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$y=\\frac{x}{1-x}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "No stationary points.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}y'&=\\frac{(1-x)+x}{(1-x)^2}\\\\y'&=\\frac{1}{(1-x)^2}\\end{align*}$$ The derivative is positive for every $x\\ne 1$. The function is undefined at $x=1$, so there are no stationary points.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 18
      }
    ]
  },
